Permission allow rule (../../../.claude/settings.json): Write(.claude/**) is not matched by file permission checks — only Edit(path) rules are. Use Edit(.claude/**) instead (Edit rules cover all file-editing tools).
Done. `auro-select` now exposes `aria-invalid` to assistive tech when validation fails.

**The placement matters here.** `auro-select`'s `role="combobox"` doesn't live on the select host — it's on the `#trigger` div inside `auro-dropdown`'s shadow root (`auro-dropdown.js:1349`). Setting `aria-invalid` on the host would have left the role and the state on different elements, with nothing associating them (CS-A11Y-001). So the attribute is bound declaratively in the dropdown's `render()`, directly beside `role`:

- `components/dropdown/src/auro-dropdown.js` — new private `get triggerInvalid()` plus an `aria-invalid` binding next to `role`/`aria-expanded`/`aria-haspopup`. It's suppressed when `triggerContentFocusable` is set (combobox/datepicker put `auro-input` in the trigger, and that input already carries its own `aria-invalid`) and when the role is `button`, which doesn't support the attribute (CS-A11Y-003). Select already mirrors its validity onto the dropdown's `error` property, both declaratively and in `performUpdate()`, so no new plumbing was needed.

- `components/select/src/auro-select.js` — added `get isInvalid()` (`validity && validity !== 'valid'`) and routed the four inlined copies of that predicate through it: the three layout renders' `?error` bindings, `renderHtmlHelpText()`, and `performUpdate()`. It's keyed on `validity`, not the `error` attribute, so `valueMissing` on a required-and-empty select is covered; the shape matches `auro-radio-group`'s existing getter rather than inventing a third expression (CS-A11Y-002).

**Tests** — four in `components/dropdown/test` (present with error + a supporting role, removed when error clears, absent for `button`, absent when the slotted content owns the role) and four in `components/select/test` (`valueMissing`, `error` attribute → `customError`, cleared on selection, absent before validation runs). I also strengthened the existing "should not set aria-invalid when blur is suppressed by noValidate" test, which was asserting on the host and would have passed no matter what the trigger did.

Select 585 passed, dropdown 370, combobox and datepicker (954) still green; `useAccessibleIt`'s axe check runs on every one of those. Source lint clean.

Sibling audit: `auro-radio-group` and `auro-checkbox-group` already have this; combobox and datepicker inherit it from `auro-input`. Not committed — let me know if you want a branch and commit.
